# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The two entries that matter most are node_modules and .env.
#
# node_modules: both Dockerfiles run `pnpm install` inside the image and then
# `COPY . .`. Without this file that COPY drops a Windows/macOS node_modules
# tree on top of the Linux one just installed, and @node-rs/argon2 — a native
# module — is then the wrong binary for the platform. Password hashing fails at
# runtime, not at build time.
#
# .env: a build context is baked into image layers. A secret copied in is still
# recoverable from the image even if a later layer deletes it.

# Dependencies — always installed inside the image, never copied in
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.production.example

# Build output — regenerated in the image
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/src/generated

# Uploads live in a volume, not in the image
storage
uploads

# Version control and tooling noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
skills-lock.json

# Test and log output
coverage
*.log

# Docs and deployment descriptors the runtime does not read
docs
README.md
CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
render.yaml
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
